@startuml
title Smart City Waste Management - Route Generation

autonumber

actor Admin
participant "Web Frontend" as Web
participant "Auth & User Service" as Auth
participant "Route Optimization Engine" as Route
participant "Request Service" as Request
participant "Fleet Service" as Fleet
participant "Facility Service" as Facility
participant "Map Service\n(OpenStreetMap)" as Map
database "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB

Admin -> Web: Request route generation for date
Web -> Auth: Validate user identity and role
Auth --> Web: Authorization result

alt User is authorized
    Web -> Route: Generate routes for selected date

    Route -> Request: Fetch approved requests for date
    Request -> DB: Query approved requests
    DB --> Request: Approved request records
    Request --> Route: Approved requests with locations and priorities

    Route -> Fleet: Fetch available vehicles and capacities
    Fleet -> DB: Query available vehicle records
    DB --> Fleet: Vehicle records
    Fleet --> Route: Available vehicles and capacities

    Route -> Facility: Fetch suitable disposal facilities
    Facility -> DB: Query facility records
    DB --> Facility: Facility records
    Facility --> Route: Facility locations and details

    Route -> Map: Obtain geographic information as required
    Map --> Route: Map/geographic information

    note over Route
      Order stops by priority,
      then shortest distance.
      Respect vehicle capacity.
      When full, direct the vehicle
      to the nearest suitable facility.
    end note

    Route -> DB: Save generated routes and stop order
    DB --> Route: Persistence result
    Route --> Web: Generated routes and ordered stops
    Web --> Admin: Display route-generation result

else User is not authorized
    Auth --> Web: Access denied
    Web --> Admin: Display authorization error
end

@enduml
